@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Customer journey 1: inference request and streamed response
actor Customer as C
boundary "Public NGINX\nAPI edge" as E
boundary "GCP HTTPS ingress\nCloud Run boundary" as L
participant "InferenceProxy\napplication" as P
participant "Identity / org services\nSupabase / controller" as A
database "Redis\nauth / route / cache" as R
participant "Kubernetes Service / routing\nVPN where applicable" as N
participant "vLLM or Dynamo\nmodel endpoint" as M
participant "CPU / GPU\nRAM, VRAM, KV cache" as G
participant "External inference\nprovider (conditional)" as X

C -[#16803C]> E : [ENC] HTTPS: API key + prompt / attachments
E -[#D4A000]> L : [CHECK] HTTPS upstream; server certificate\nverification not enabled in reviewed NGINX config (F09)
L -[#DC2626]> P : [PLAIN] Managed container boundary: h2c\nTLS already terminated; not an Internet plaintext hop
group Authenticate and authorize before dispatch (logical dependencies)
P -[#D4A000]> A : [CHECK] Resolve caller / organization / entitlement\nExact cache-hit and identity-service path varies
note over P,A
API key / JWT authentication is separate from encryption.
This group is a dependency view, not a claim that every
request makes every identity-service call.
end note
P -[#DC2626]> R : [PLAIN] redis:// with password; private networking\nAuth/routing/cache operations as needed
R -[#16803C]> R : [ENC] GCP storage-layer encryption for persistence\nNo per-tenant key boundary established
end
alt Request served by an internal deployment
P -[#D4A000]> N : [CHECK] HTTPS + private CA, deployment bearer token\nShared long-lived wildcard identity (F07)
N -[#D4A000]> M : [CHECK] Forward TLS ciphertext to model endpoint\nRouter / Service does not terminate application TLS
note over N,M
Tailscale adds WireGuard only on routes using its peers.
vLLM enforces the deployment token; Dynamo omits it (F08).
Dynamo frontend HTTPS exists; internal graph/event links
need separate authentication/encryption evidence.
end note
M -[#DC2626]> M : [PLAIN] Endpoint decrypts prompt into application memory
M -[#D4A000]> G : [CHECK] Tokenization / tensors / KV cache / generation\nCPU-GPU link and RAM/VRAM protection not attested
G -[#D4A000]> M : [CHECK] Generated tokens; hardware isolation unknown
M -[#D4A000]> P : [CHECK] Stream over same HTTPS session / routing\nShared TLS identity caveat remains
else Organization policy permits external offload
P -[#16803C]> X : [ENC] HTTPS: prompt + provider credential
X -[#D4A000]> X : [CHECK] Provider processing, storage and retention\nSite, memory protection and key custody not established
X -[#16803C]> P : [ENC] HTTPS response stream
end
P -[#DC2626]> L : [PLAIN] Response at local managed h2c boundary
L -[#D4A000]> E : [CHECK] Response on upstream TLS connection (F09)
E -[#16803C]> C : [ENC] HTTPS: streamed answer
note over P,G
Processes necessarily see plaintext. Host/admin access is not
excluded by TLS. This diagram does not claim every prompt
is stored in Redis or queued through RabbitMQ.
end note
@enduml
